ion\'s attitudinal/psychological causal claim is unsupported by these citations."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spatial_cognition", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Wikipedia article describes spatial scale distinctions (figural to geographical), how people learn and navigate larger environments, and correlations between spatial abilities and wayfinding attitudes (sense of direction, spatial self-efficacy, pleasure in exploring). It does not provide evidence that operating at larger spatial scales causes people to develop a more proactive attitude, greater sense of responsibility, or forward-thinking behavior. At best the article notes task demands (planning/decision in wayfinding) and associations with self-reported attitudes, but it contains no causal claim or data that increasing spatial scale directly produces a psychological shift toward proactivity or responsibility."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Increasing the spatial scale at which individuals operate directly causes them to develop a more proactive attitude, as dealing with larger areas enhances their sense of responsibility and initiative. Exposure to broader spatial challenges supposedly triggers a psychological shift towards greater forward-thinking behavior.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing the spatial scale at which individuals operate directly causes them to develop a more proactive attitude, as dealing with larger areas enhances their sense of responsibility and initiative. Exposure to broader spatial challenges supposedly triggers a psychological shift towards greater forward-thinking behavior.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

