ediated by other factors. Therefore the citation does not substantiate the explanation\'s negative causal claim."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Chronic addiction does not directly cause financial barriers, nor do financial barriers directly cause chronic addiction. Any association between these variables is likely mediated by other factors such as healthcare costs or employment status, which are not direct causal pathways. No direct causal mechanism exists between chronic addiction and financial barriers in the absence of mediating variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.3586761216418834, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8087394456644798, 'min_prob': 0.04043300379179756, 'token_prob_slope': -0.005265596901915832, 'prob_variance': 0.06172016978766226, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.037708084615236, 'avg_nll': 0.3065107856783733}

