ned (\'None\')\\" variables nor does it support asserting a definitive absence of causation solely from lack of definitions; it only supports that causality cannot be inferred without appropriate data.  \\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.5"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK571451/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited NIDA report documents substantial links between substance use disorders (chronic addiction) and multiple co-occurring physical and mental health conditions (multimorbidity), including discussion of pathways by which substance use can contribute to development or worsening of other illnesses and how physical/mental conditions can increase risk of SUD. Therefore the claim that there is \\"no\\" relationship or causal basis is contradicted by the source material."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3384512/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article describes addiction as a chronic, often-relapsing disorder and explicitly discusses links between substance use/addiction and multiple morbidity and mental-health outcomes (e.g., increased risk for other psychological problems, mortality and morbidity associated with alcohol use). It presents multilevel, bidirectional influences rather than asserting no relationship. It does not support the claim that there is no causal or associative relationship between chronic addiction and multi-morbidity; if anything it indicates relationships and shared risk mechanisms."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Chronic addiction does not cause multi-morbidity or vice versa in this case because both variables are undefined ('None'), so there is no basis for a causal relationship between them.", 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.357103212242513, 'mean_t