   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.22564717656427696, 'citations': ['https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://medlineplus.gov/druguseandaddiction.html', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud', 'https://nida.nih.gov/publications/drugfacts/understanding-drug-use-addiction'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7858528337303254, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Cleveland Clinic source describes addiction as a chronic condition and lists causes and risk factors (genetics, mental health, environmental exposures) and notes that addiction can impair functioning at work and school. It does not state that education level and chronic addiction have no direct causal relationship; in fact it implies addiction can directly harm schooling/education-related functioning. The citation therefore does not support the claim that there is no direct causal relationship in either direction.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Cleveland Clinic source explicitly says substance use disorder can \\"significantly impact ... education and career\\" and lists \\"academic or career challenges\\" as a common complication; it also notes that education/prevention programs can reduce risk of developing SUD. Those statements support causal influence of chronic addiction on education outcomes (and of education interventions on SUD risk), so the claim that there is no direct causal relationship in either direction is