 as influencing risk. Those statements suggest plausible causal links or pathways between addiction and education-related factors, so the source does not support the claim of no direct causal relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Chronic addiction does not directly cause education level to change, nor does education level directly cause chronic addiction. While there may be associations or mediating factors, there is no direct causal relationship between these variables in either direction.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.23449719683342, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8575053869099231, 'min_prob': 0.15667660873523434, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00587607844427606, 'prob_variance': 0.050916648291429986, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8050418091525458, 'avg_nll': 0.2106637591107014}

