   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.23665505982556412, 'citations': ['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation_does_not_imply_causation', 'https://opentext.wsu.edu/abnormal-psych/chapter/module-14-neurocognitive-disorders/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6519631/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557444/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/neuroscience/cognitive-disorders'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7707087692926806, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation_does_not_imply_causation", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited Wikipedia article explains the general principle that correlation alone does not establish causation and that demonstrating causality requires time ordering, plausible mechanisms, and ruling out confounders. That supports the explanation\'s methodological point that a defined mechanism or evidence is needed before claiming causation. However, the source does not provide any direct evidence regarding the specific relationship between \\"Cognitive disorder\\" and \\"Personnel\\" nor does it demonstrate that no causal link exists between them. Therefore the citation only partially supports the claim."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://opentext.wsu.edu/abnormal-psych/chapter/module-14-neurocognitive-disorders/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited module describes neurocognitive disorders—their clinical presentation, etiologies (e.g., Alzheimer’s, TBI, vascular causes), epidemiology, and treatments—but it does not mention or define \\"Personnel\\" nor discuss any causal links between neurocognitive disorders and personnel/employee variables. Because the sources contain no information addressing the relationship, they do not provide evidence that no causal link exists."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.