atedly describes frailty as a loss of physiological reserve and functioning (reduced \\"reserve capacity\\" and functional status), and links frailty to impaired physical function and associations with cognitive impairment. That directly implies a relationship between frailty and capacity, so the claim of \\"NONE\\" is not supported by the sources."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/frailty", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Cleveland Clinic source describes frailty as reduced ability to withstand and recover from stressors, causing loss of independence, difficulty with activities of daily living, disability, and limited treatment options — all indicating an effect on a person\'s functional capacity. That contradicts a \\"no relationship\\" claim.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "I don't know", 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.0632081589141522, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9546904640006438, 'min_prob': 0.518132464052297, 'token_prob_slope': -0.009512873148457498, 'prob_variance': 0.019080655670209806, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.25805378584644645, 'avg_nll': 0.06129090230971909}

