isting \\"medication management\\"), and notes risk factors like polypharmacy. It does not explicitly examine or rule out causal pathways between frailty and \\"therapy compliance,\\" nor does it state that no relationship exists. Because the citation implies frailty can impair a patient\'s ability to manage/take medications (which relates to adherence/compliance) but does not provide explicit causal analysis, the claim that there is no direct relationship is only partially supported by the cited source."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Frailty does not directly cause therapy compliance, nor does therapy compliance directly cause frailty. There is no defined mechanism or directionality between these variables based on their definitions and available information. Without a clear causal link, no direct relationship should be included in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.4839650329894514, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7561335308295816, 'min_prob': 0.1275016943298541, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004128309793151275, 'prob_variance': 0.08406452690990138, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.2250838873377017, 'avg_nll': 0.39471758179201266}

