   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.25076302323476624, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4020025/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8333339089138431, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review explicitly defines \\"therapeutic compliance\\" (including medication, diet, exercise and lifestyle changes), discusses measurement issues and rates (e.g., compliance with lifestyle changes 20–30%), and identifies factors affecting compliance. It therefore contradicts the explanation\'s claim that there is no defined meaning or measurement for therapy compliance; while the paper may not analyze a single variable labelled \\"healthy lifestyle\\" as an independent predictor, it directly treats lifestyle changes as part of compliance and provides evidence on related measures and determinants. The explanation is not supported by the citation. \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4020025/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited concept-analysis paper documents that \\"compliance\\" (and related terms adherence/concordance) lack a single agreed definition and that measurement methods are inconsistent and problematic, which supports the claim that therapy compliance is not well-defined/measured. However, the source does not address the meaning or measurement of \\"healthy lifestyle,\\" nor does it state that a causal relationship between a healthy lifestyle and therapy compliance cannot be established—only that unclear definitions and measurement complicate research. Therefore the explanation is only partly supported by the provided citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "There is no defined meaning or measurement for either 'Healthy lifestyle' or 'Therapy compliance', so no direct causal relationship can be established between them.", 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.257142321888556, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8611547928990674, 'min_prob': 0.16523106514524952, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0017610017586579018, 'prob_variance': 0.0628820938218399, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.6464293538196403, 'avg_nll': 0.22884114665829003}

