th, functioning, and quality of life, but it does not address whether an individual\'s healthy lifestyle does or does not directly change the functioning of healthcare professionals, nor does it provide evidence that any relationship is mediated by acute care demand or capacity. The citation therefore does not support the claim denying a direct causal link between healthy lifestyle and healthcare professionals\' functioning."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "Healthy lifestyle does not directly cause functioning of healthcare professionals to change. While healthier populations might indirectly affect healthcare demands, there is no direct causal mechanism by which an individual's healthy lifestyle directly changes the functioning of healthcare professionals. Any apparent association is likely mediated by other variables such as acute care demand or capacity, so no direct causal link should be drawn in the CLD.", 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.5179227391808223, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7745354336860854, 'min_prob': 0.02458911315942519, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0021418212329310177, 'prob_variance': 0.08527465784272051, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9300369701399979, 'avg_nll': 0.4173427812228484}

