ov/articles/PMC5880778/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited qualitative study explicitly reports that financial strain shapes health decision-making — participants described foregoing or delaying medical care, using alternative remedies, and prioritizing household needs because of limited financial resources. That indicates a direct causal pathway from financial resources (financial strain) to healthcare avoidance. The citation does not support the claim that there is no direct relationship; it provides evidence of at least one directional effect.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.healthsystemtracker.org/chart-collection/cost-affect-access-care/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited KFF analysis directly links financial resources to healthcare avoidance: it reports that adults with incomes below 200% of the federal poverty level are nearly twice as likely to delay or go without care due to cost, uninsured adults delay care far more than insured adults, and many people worry about or experience medical bills. The source therefore supports a direct effect of financial resources (income/insurance status) on healthcare avoidance and also shows that healthcare costs can affect household finances (medical bills, debt). This contradicts the claim of no direct causal relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Healthcare avoidance does not directly cause financial resources to change, nor do financial resources directly cause healthcare avoidance to change within the given definitions and context. Any apparent association would likely be mediated by other variables such as financial barriers or access to care, which are already included in the CLD. Therefore, there is no direct causal relationship between these two variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2946210031046719, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8510040056317679, 'min_prob': 0.06126963362106163, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0006819327729867749, 'prob_variance': 0.06274016588987148, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1255368835436903, 'avg_nll': 0.25821799062247563}

