   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.2160974405387676, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/', 'https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2656/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8614640/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8444254429927222, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited StatPearls article thoroughly describes incorrect medication use (types, causes, consequences, prevention) but contains no discussion of \\"spatial scale\\" nor any mechanism linking medication misuse to changes in spatial scale. Because the sources provide information about medication errors only and do not mention or connect to spatial scale, the claim that there is no relationship is supported by the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2656/", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited chapter thoroughly documents causes, rates, and system/process factors related to medication errors but does not discuss \\"spatial scale\\" as a variable or suggest any causal link between incorrect medication use and changes in spatial scale (nor the reverse). There is no content in the source that supports a causal or direct association between these concepts, so the claim of no relationship is consistent with the citation material."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation discusses causes, prevention, and systems related to medication errors but contains no information about \\"spatial scale\\" or any relationship (causal or non-causal) between medication use/errors and spatial scale. Beca