   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.2633497708588016, 'citations': ['https://aspe.hhs.gov/medication-decisions-right-wrong', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/', 'https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2723196/', 'https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/08870446.2022.2144923'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.6864888998256926, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://aspe.hhs.gov/medication-decisions-right-wrong", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited report documents many clinical harms and downstream health consequences of inappropriate or incorrect medication use (adverse reactions, hospitalizations, institutionalization) and describes patient-level mediators of misuse (e.g., low socioeconomic status, poor compliance, health literacy, prescribing/pricing factors). However, it does not examine or provide evidence about effects of incorrect medication use specifically on “healthy lifestyle” behaviors (diet, exercise, smoking, etc.), nor does it demonstrate a lack of any direct causal pathway. It does support the idea that associations with medication misuse are often mediated by factors like socioeconomic status and patient behavior, but it does not directly substantiate the stronger claim that no direct causal relationship to healthy lifestyle exists."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited StatPearls article documents that medication errors cause patient harm and adverse clinical outcomes and discusses causes and prevention (including patient education and communication). It does not evaluate or provide evidence about effects on \\"healthy lifestyle,\\" nor does it demonstrate the absence of a direct causal pathway between incorrect medication use and healthy lifestyle or show that any association is mediated by factors like health literacy. Therefore the citation does not support the claim that there is no direct relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited AMCP material documents that medication errors and incorrect medication use cause patient harm, morbidity, and economic costs and discusses prevention and patient education; it does not discuss the relationship (or lack of one) between incorrect medication use and the broader construct \\"healthy lifestyle\\" or claim that no direct causal mechanism exists. Therefore the explanation—that there is no direct causal effect on healthy lifestyle—is not supported by the provided source content."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2723196/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article defines and classifies medication errors and discusses their causes and prevention, but it does not address effects on or causal relationships with \\"healthy lifestyle\\" nor mentions mediators like health literacy or education in relation to lifestyle. Therefore the explanation\'s claim that incorrect medication use has no direct causal effect on healthy lifestyle (and that any association would be mediated by other factors) is not supported by the provided citation.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication does not directly cause healthy lifestyle to change. There is no established causal mechanism by which incorrect use of medication would directly increase or decrease a healthy lifestyle, and no directionality is supported between these variables. Any possible association would likely be mediated by other factors such as health literacy or education level, which are already present in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.4182673634251444, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7849621551305795, 'min_prob': 0.020326939171454974, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0016770780521183474, 'prob_variance': 0.06935310181138332, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.2445549100226008, 'avg_nll': 0.3494359600018046}

