821. Language and cultural barriers-[POSITIVE]->Care avoidance behavior
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause care avoidance behavior in a direct causal relationship. When language and cultural barriers increase, individuals are more likely to avoid seeking care due to communication difficulties or cultural misunderstandings. Conversely, reducing these barriers makes people less likely to avoid care. This relationship does not require mediation by variables already present in the CLD.', 'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.25568308122064703, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515484/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7786751/', 'https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/language-barriers-and-patient-encounter/2007-08'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8273800754192264, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515484/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited qualitative study documents that language and cultural barriers hinder communication, produce uncertainty and relational disconnect, and can reduce engagement with care — findings that are consistent with increased avoidance or reduced use of services. However, the article reports these barriers mainly from general practitioners’ perspectives and does not provide evidence for the specific mechanism proposed (that affected individuals have an intrinsic stronger desire for self-reliance/independence and therefore manage health issues themselves). The claim’s core causal explanation (self-reliance as the driver of avoidance) is not supported by the provided source."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7786751/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article documents that language and cultural discordance can reduce use of health and social services (e.g., 