 stress responses that weaken immunity or biologically predispose individuals to develop multiple chronic diseases irrespective of other factors. The specific biological mechanism and causal link to multi-morbidity are not supported by the source."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.qualityhealth.org/wpsc/2017/10/13/impact-of-language-cultural-barriers-on-patient-safety-health-equity/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article documents that language and cultural barriers worsen access to care, increase communication failures, reduce preventive screening, and lead to adverse medical events and health disparities — supporting a link to poorer health outcomes and potentially greater disease burden. However, it does not provide evidence that these barriers directly cause physiological stress responses that weaken the immune system or biologically predispose individuals to develop multi-morbidity independent of other social or lifestyle factors. The specific biological causal mechanism and direct link to multi-morbidity are not demonstrated in the source."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32423835/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited paper discusses difficulties in intercultural health communication and strategies to mitigate language and cultural barriers to reduce health disparities and improve care. It does not provide evidence that these barriers directly produce physiological stress responses that weaken the immune system or biologically predispose people to develop multiple chronic diseases independent of other social or lifestyle factors. Therefore the source does not support the specific biological causal mechanism or the claim of a direct increase in multi-morbidity risk as stated."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers directly 