   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.24624445007840645, 'citations': ['https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/mental-illness/symptoms-causes/syc-20374968', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK20369/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2174594/', 'https://www.psychiatry.org/patients-families/what-is-mental-illness', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/22295-mental-health-disorders'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8273193449406322, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/mental-illness/symptoms-causes/syc-20374968", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Mayo Clinic page describes causes, symptoms, risk factors, and complications of mental illness but does not mention \\"24/7-care mentality\\" or address any causal link between that concept and mental disorders. It therefore does not provide evidence that no direct causal relationship exists (nor does it provide evidence of one). The cited source neither establishes nor rules out the claimed absence of a causal mechanism, so it does not support the explanation."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK20369/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited NIH curriculum text describes what mental illnesses are, their symptoms, impacts on functioning, risk factors, treatment, and stigma (including the stereotype that people \\"need somebody to take care of them\\"), but it does not discuss a concept called \\"24/7‑care mentality\\" or provide evidence that there is no direct causal link in either direction. The source actually notes that severe mental illnesses can impair functioning and may lead to increased need for services or care, so it does not support the strong claim that no causal mechanism exists. Therefore the explanation is not supported by the cited material."}, {"citati