gid/hierarchical organizational structures to direct causation of cognitive disorders. Because the citation contains no viewable material, it does not support the explanation."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://openstax.org/books/principles-management/pages/4-3-organizational-designs-and-structures", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The OpenStax chapter describes types of organizational structures and notes workplace disadvantages (e.g., rigid hierarchies, isolation, feelings of being \\"out of control,\\" reduced autonomy, coordination problems), but it does not provide empirical evidence or discussion linking those structures to chronic stress causing neurological changes or to development of cognitive disorders (dementia, memory impairment). There are no citations in the provided source that support a causal relationship between hierarchical organizational design and clinical cognitive disorders."}], "aggregate_score": 0.16666666666666666, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Rigid and hierarchical organizational structures can directly cause cognitive disorders in employees by creating environments of chronic stress and reduced autonomy. Over time, the lack of flexibility and empowerment in such workplaces leads to neurological changes that increase the risk of developing cognitive disorders such as dementia or memory impairment.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.16666666666666666, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Rigid and hierarchical organizational structures can directly cause cognitive disorders in employees by creating environments of chronic stress and reduced autonomy. Over time, the lack of flexibility and empowerment in such workplaces leads to neurological changes that increase the risk of developing cognitive disorders such as dementia or memory impairment.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

