rsonnel\\" nor provide any evidence that \\"Personnel\\" causes (or is caused by) frailty. Therefore the conclusion that no causal link is identified is supported by the absence of any supporting evidence in the citation. However, the explanation incorrectly states that \\"Frailty\\" is undefined — the source does define frailty — so the explanation\'s justification is not fully aligned with the citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.3, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Without definitions for 'Personnel' and 'Frailty', it is not possible to establish a causal relationship. There is no clear mechanism indicating that 'Personnel' causes 'Frailty' or vice versa. Therefore, no direct causal link can be identified between these variables.", 'aggregate_score': 0.3, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3053121815691195, 'mean_token_prob': 0.865000652442757, 'min_prob': 0.01161742871875302, 'token_prob_slope': 0.0006878960721610835, 'prob_variance': 0.060904609740178785, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7914171271724441, 'avg_nll': 0.26644223175940723}

