1133. Therapy compliance-[NONE]->Knowledge
   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.310582759243178, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4592639/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2212144724000991', 'https://www.hhs.nd.gov/sites/www/files/documents/BH/cuijpers_2019_annurev-clinpsy-common-factors.pdf'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7186323828280384, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review explicitly lists patient knowledge and health literacy as factors that affect therapeutic compliance and discusses how patient education and understanding can improve adherence. That supports a causal pathway from knowledge → compliance. The review does not support the claim that there is \\"no direct causal relationship\\"; it directly contradicts it (even if it acknowledges mediators and complexity). It does not, however, provide evidence that compliance causes changes in knowledge, but the explanation claimed no causal relationship in either direction. Overall the citations do not support the assertion of no direct causal effect (at least knowledge → compliance is supported by the source)."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4592639/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article reviews common factors in psychotherapy (alliance, empathy, expectations, adherence/competence, etc.) and reports that adherence/competence show minimal effects on clinical outcomes. It does not investigate or report on \\"knowledge\\" as an outcome or on causal pathways between therapy compliance and knowledge. Therefore the citation does not provide direct evidence that therapy compliance does not cause changes in knowledge (nor that knowledge does not causally affect compliance); at best it addresses adherence effects on clinical symptom outcomes, not the specific variables named in the claim."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2212144724000991", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source contains an error message and provides no usable content or evidence about the relationship between therapy compliance and knowledge, so it does not support the explanation.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.hhs.nd.gov/sites/www/files/documents/BH/cuijpers_2019_annurev-clinpsy-common-factors.pdf", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review emphasizes that psychotherapy mechanisms and mediators are largely unestablished, that causal pathways require temporal, dose–response and experimental evidence, and that many patient-level moderators/mediators (extratherapeutic factors) can confound apparent effects. That supports the general claim that direct causal mechanisms between two specific variables (here, therapy compliance and patient knowledge) are not established and that indirect paths or third variables are plausible. However, the article does not specifically analyze \\"therapy compliance\\" or \\"knowledge\\" nor provide direct evidence that no causal link exists between them. Therefore the citation supports the general reasoning about lack of proven direct mechanisms but does not specifically confirm the stated null relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Therapy compliance does not cause knowledge to change, nor does knowledge cause therapy compliance to change in a direct causal manner. There is no established mechanism by which therapy compliance directly influences knowledge. Without a direct pathway and considering possible mediators like health literacy or education level, no direct causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.572503345292135, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7637665113678908, 'min_prob': 0.05412007123415492, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003875785242892545, 'prob_variance': 0.09646165033910588, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1355522078166804, 'avg_nll': 0.45266883696198273}

