   Properties: {'session_id': '1bbf851c-0fd8-4beb-8ae0-b4dcf706c376', 'prob_std': 0.21985747761289728, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/', 'https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors', 'https://psnet.ahrq.gov/web-mm/wrong-time-error-high-alert-medication', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2656/', 'https://aspe.hhs.gov/medication-decisions-right-wrong'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8207803875500518, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The StatPearls article explicitly identifies time-related problems (e.g., \\"Incorrect Timing\\", \\"Incorrect Duration\\", wrong rate of administration) as common types and causes of medication errors and discusses timing/scheduling accuracy as a challenge. Thus the citation contradicts the claim that there is no relationship between time and incorrect use of medication."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2656/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited chapter directly links time-related factors to medication errors: it identifies \\"wrong time\\" as a common type of medication administration error, presents error rates both including and excluding wrong-time errors, and reports associations between nurses\' working hours/shift length (e.g., >12.5 hours) and increased medication errors. It also shows that adverse drug events from medication errors can increase length of stay (i.e., time in hospital). Therefore the sources contradict the blanket claim that \\"time\\" has no relationship with incorrect medication use. The evidence does not support labeling the relationship NONE. \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited AMCP source describes time-related factors that can contribute to medication errors (e.g., failure to administer a drug \\"in a timely manner,\\" instructions on \\"when is the best time to take it\\" and \\"how long to take it,\\" and inclusion of expiration dates in bar codes). Those passages indicate temporal issues (timing, delays, duration, expiry) can be mechanisms leading to incorrect medication use, so the blanket claim that \\"time does not cause incorrect use of medication\\" is not supported by the citation.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://psnet.ahrq.gov/web-mm/wrong-time-error-high-alert-medication", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source is an Amazon CloudFront error page (403) with no substantive content about time or medication use. It provides no evidence or discussion relevant to whether time and incorrect use of medication are causally related, so it cannot support the explanation.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://aspe.hhs.gov/medication-decisions-right-wrong", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited report documents time-related patterns and temporal effects on inappropriate medication use (e.g., changes in prescribing after clinical trial evidence, comparisons of 1989 vs 1996 prescribing, and discussion of temporal trends and the need for longer timeframes). It therefore does not support a blanket claim that \\"time\\" has no relationship to incorrect medication use; if anything it presents evidence that temporal factors and trends can be associated with improper use and that time-based research is needed. The explanation\'s assertion of no direct causal relationship is not supported by the provided source material."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Time does not cause incorrect use of medication, nor does incorrect use of medication cause time. Without a specific context or mechanism linking these variables, there is no direct causal relationship between them.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2156929142555453, 'mean_token_prob': 0.870912764433606, 'min_prob': 0.12008963586266007, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0035139724574527356, 'prob_variance': 0.048337310462305626, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9582144145087821, 'avg_nll': 0.19531421403218618}

