ord.edu/king-papers/documents/draft-chapter-xiv-mastery-fear-or-antidotes-fear", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The MLK sermon repeatedly links the current historical moment (\\"our time,\\" \\"age of fear,\\" \\"these days of terrifying change\\") and specific time‑period phenomena (atomic weapons, economic automation, arms races) to increases in fear; it discusses causes and remedies for fear but does not state that there is no causal relationship between \\"time\\" and fear. Because the citation actually connects features of a given time period to heightened fear, it does not support the claim that there is no causal or contextual link between time and feelings of fear (and it does not address shame in a way that affirms the \\"none\\" claim either)."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Time does not cause feelings of fear and shame, nor do feelings of fear and shame cause time to change. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these variables in either direction based on their definitions.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.3146050644763223, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8765850068645813, 'min_prob': 0.013111910836994799, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00771190413482141, 'prob_variance': 0.05440430211022952, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7989404024174129, 'avg_nll': 0.2735362893245691}

