ption, interoperability gaps, privacy/cybersecurity, workforce and incentive misalignment) and does not claim that a \\"24/7‑care mentality\\" by itself will automatically cause organizations to develop advanced information systems or make information universally accessible. Thus the citation supports the basic link between continuous/around‑the‑clock care needs and the requirement for more accessible digital information, but not the stronger causal/automatic claim in the explanation."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/social-sciences/access-to-information", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source content is unavailable (Cloudflare/error message) and provides no evidence for the claimed relationship. There is nothing in the provided citation to show that a 24/7-care mentality increases information accessibility or leads to more advanced information systems."}], "aggregate_score": 0.16666666666666666, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality directly increases the accessibility of information because constant care requires immediate access to data at all times. As a result, organizations with this mentality will automatically develop more advanced information systems, making information more accessible to everyone.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.16666666666666666, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality directly increases the accessibility of information because constant care requires immediate access to data at all times. As a result, organizations with this mentality will automatically develop more advanced information systems, making information more accessible to everyone.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

