sions, or any mechanism whereby anticipated higher demand leads administrators to reduce available capacity. There is no evidence in the citation supporting a policy-driven negative effect of increased ED demand on Capacity as claimed."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit negatively impacts Capacity because as the emergency department anticipates higher demand, administrators proactively reduce the number of available beds and staff allocations to prevent potential overcrowding and maintain quality standards. Thus, increased acute care demand leading to an ED visit results in a policy-driven decrease in Capacity, whereas lower demand prompts administrators to expand Capacity by making additional resources available.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit negatively impacts Capacity because as the emergency department anticipates higher demand, administrators proactively reduce the number of available beds and staff allocations to prevent potential overcrowding and maintain quality standards. Thus, increased acute care demand leading to an ED visit results in a policy-driven decrease in Capacity, whereas lower demand prompts administrators to expand Capacity by making additional resources available.', 'perplexity': 1.4147655547657312, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8093291596809132, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.036169534009087394, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004969224742476827, 'prob_variance': 0.0738077150605097, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9050616553881831, 'avg_nll': 0.34696383168988426}

