   Properties: {'session_id': '62897d48-baff-417b-a11c-f996ae0fb098', 'prob_std': 0.23369048433854117, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3169799/', 'https://us.sagepub.com/sites/default/files/upm-binaries/23639_Chapter_5___Causation_and_Experimental_Design.pdf', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5880718/', 'https://nam.edu/perspectives/understanding-the-relationship-between-education-and-health/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8062147310348489, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3169799/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review directly treats education as an SES component, provides measures (e.g., education categories), empirical associations (Table 1 odds ratios showing large education gradients for smoking and physical inactivity), and discusses multiple causal mechanisms linking education/SES to health behaviors. Far from saying no definitions or data exist, the paper documents and analyzes the relationship between education and health-related behaviors. Therefore the claim of \\"NONE\\" due to lack of definitions/measurements is contradicted by the source."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5880718/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review summarizes extensive empirical evidence that higher educational attainment is linked to better health and longer life, explicitly defines education (attainment, years/credentials), identifies health behaviors (lifestyle) as a major mediating pathway, and discusses causal studies (natural experiments, twin designs). Therefore the sources contradict the claim of \\"no relationship\\" and the explanation about missing definitions/mechanisms is not supported by the citations.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "No defi