//www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0272735820300209", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation contains only an error message and no substantive content to evaluate. There is no evidence in the cited material that addresses causal (or non-causal) links between frailty and financial barriers, mediators, or mechanisms. Because the citation provides no usable information, it cannot support the claim that there is no direct causal relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37979598/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited paper examines bidirectional causal links between frailty and mental disorders (e.g., major depressive disorder, ASRD) using Mendelian randomization; it does not analyze or report on financial barriers. Therefore it provides no evidence for or against a causal relationship between frailty and financial barriers and cannot support the claim that no direct causal relationship exists between those variables."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Frailty does not cause financial barriers, nor do financial barriers cause frailty in a direct causal manner. There is no established direct causal mechanism between these two variables; any observed association would likely be due to mediating variables such as health literacy or financial resources. Therefore, no direct causal relationship should be included in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.340942281651588, 'mean_token_prob': 0.820448718929115, 'min_prob': 0.04364722211350794, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0031056108088040207, 'prob_variance': 0.06874722546584455, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0047490242783004, 'avg_nll': 0.2933725620992556}

