luding cultural and conceptual knowledge and affecting understanding of illness, medications, and access to information. It discusses links between limited health literacy and reduced understanding and health outcomes. Therefore the source does not support a \\"no relationship\\" claim between health literacy and knowledge — it implies a substantive relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.nnlm.gov/guides/intro-health-literacy", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited NNLM source defines health literacy as the ability to find, understand, appraise, and use health information and explicitly links higher health literacy with being more informed and making well‑informed health decisions. That indicates a clear relationship between health literacy and knowledge/information, so the claim of \\"no relationship\\" is not supported by the citation.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://odphp.health.gov/healthypeople/priority-areas/health-literacy-healthy-people-2030", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Healthy People 2030 citation defines personal health literacy as the ability to find, understand, and use information to inform health decisions — explicitly linking health literacy to understanding information (i.e., knowledge-related abilities). It provides no evidence that health literacy is unrelated to knowledge; rather it implies a clear connection.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "I don't know", 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.0167965844798796, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9845128375562968, 'min_prob': 0.8490904704624713, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003619930677366952, 'prob_variance': 0.001864422099613692, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.12465722249956789, 