643. Health literacy-[NONE]->Frailty
   Properties: {'session_id': '62897d48-baff-417b-a11c-f996ae0fb098', 'prob_std': 0.23713592027063293, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2020.00280/full', 'https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0303164', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35886562/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1492599/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7834880805303829, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article reviews links between health literacy and many health outcomes (hospitalizations, mortality, disease self-management, screening, obesity, etc.) but does not mention or provide data on frailty. Because the sources do not address frailty, they do not support the claim that there is no relationship between health literacy and frailty (nor any claim about their relationship)."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1492599/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited systematic review examines links between reading/health literacy and many health outcomes (knowledge, hospitalization, chronic disease control, ADLs in specific conditions, global health measures) but does not assess \\"frailty\\" as a defined outcome. Because the evidence does not address frailty directly, it cannot be used to support a conclusion of \\"no relationship.\\" (The review even reports several associations between low literacy and worse health or function in other domains, so absence of a frailty-specific analysis is not evidence of no effect.)  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2020.00280/full", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited study does not report \\"no relationship.\\" Although the SEM found no direct path from health literacy to frailty, it reports a statistically significant indirect (and total) negative association of health literacy with frailty mediated by social support and depression; the regression analysis also identified health literacy as an influencing factor. Thus the evidence shows an association (indirect), not absence of any relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0303164", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited PLOS ONE study reports a statistically significant negative correlation between frailty and health literacy (r = -0.27, p < .001) and discusses prior work linking low health literacy to greater frailty and frailty progression. Thus the provided sources indicate an association (and suggest predictive relationships), not \\"no relationship.\\" The explanation given (lack of definitions) does not match the evidence in the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35886562/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited study reports that high health literacy and regular exercise were protective factors and concludes poor health literacy is a risk factor for prefrailty and frailty in a large national sample. That directly indicates an association (and the authors characterize health literacy as a risk factor), so the claim of \\"no relationship / cannot determine\\" is not supported by the citation.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "I don't know the definitions of 'Health literacy' or 'Frailty' as provided, so I cannot determine if a causal relationship exists between them.", 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2679670806