648. Healthy lifestyle-[POSITIVE]->Willingness of social network
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle does not cause willingness of social network, and willingness of social network does not cause healthy lifestyle within the information provided. There is no established direct causal mechanism linking these variables. Without specific definitions or evidence, no causal relationship can be identified.', 'session_id': '62897d48-baff-417b-a11c-f996ae0fb098', 'citations': ['https://lhsfna.org/social-wellness-the-influence-of-social-support-on-health/', 'https://www.summahealth.org/flourish/entries/2023/12/five-surprising-health-benefits-to-socializing-with-others', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/lim2.91', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3150158/', 'https://www.sbm.org/healthy-living/how-social-connections-benefit-healthy-living'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.summahealth.org/flourish/entries/2023/12/five-surprising-health-benefits-to-socializing-with-others", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article describes how social connections benefit an individual\'s health and how social networks can influence a person\'s healthy choices (network -> individual). It emphasizes that having supportive relationships provides emotional and practical support for the individual, and that partners/friends can encourage each other\'s healthy behaviors. It does not provide evidence that an individual adopting a healthy lifestyle directly increases their social network’s willingness to support them (individual health behavior -> increased willingness of others to help), nor that simply eating better or exercising will, by itself, make others more motivated to support you. The directionality and the strong, unconditional causal claim in the explanation are not substantiated by the source content."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3150158/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article reviews extensive evidence that social relationships influence individuals’ health and health behaviors (e.g., social control, support, and contagion) and emphasizes complex, bidirectional, and context-dependent links (including that relationships can both help and hinder health). It does not provide evidence that an individual’s adopting a healthy lifestyle by itself directly increases their network’s willingness to support them; nor does it support the absolute claim that eating better or exercising will automatically make one’s social circle more supportive without other factors. The source instead highlights that social ties shape behaviors and that effects depend on relationship quality, norms, and other social factors."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sbm.org/healthy-living/how-social-connections-benefit-healthy-living", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited SBM article describes how social connections benefit healthy living and advises including plans to strengthen social ties when pursuing health goals. It emphasizes that being socially connected helps individuals stay healthier, and offers tips for increasing quantity, quality, and diversity of relationships. It does not provide evidence that simply adopting healthy behaviors (eating better or exercising) directly increases your social network’s willingness to support you, nor does it claim that friends and family automatically become more motivated to help as a result of another person’s healthy choices. The explanation reverses the direction of the relationship and asserts an unqualified causal effect that the source does not state."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Adopting a healthy lifestyle directly increases the willingness of your social network to support you, because when you make healthy choices, your friends and family become more motivated and eager to help you succeed. This means that simply eating better or exercising will make your social circle more supportive without any other factors involved.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Adopting a healthy lifestyle directly increases the willingness of your social network to support you, because when you make healthy choices, your friends and family become more motivated and eager to help you succeed. This means that simply eating better or exercising will make your social circle more supportive without any other factors involved.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

