ggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication does not cause financial resources to change, nor does financial resources cause incorrect use of medication to change, in a direct causal manner. There is no evident direct causal mechanism linking these two variables. Any association would likely be mediated by other factors such as health outcomes or health care costs, not a direct effect. Therefore, no direct causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.475867835961552, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8014002799011747, 'min_prob': 0.0022172398732332762, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0025646900132805135, 'prob_variance': 0.06902490252780906, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9709386759477512, 'avg_nll': 0.3892461801376849}

