   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Proactive attitude causes language and cultural barriers to change in an inverse relationship. Increasing proactive attitude directly reduces language and cultural barriers by encouraging individuals to seek resources, learn, and adapt to new environments. Conversely, a decrease in proactive attitude can increase the persistence of these barriers. The causality is direct, as proactive behaviors actively work to overcome communication and cultural obstacles.', 'session_id': '62897d48-baff-417b-a11c-f996ae0fb098', 'citations': ['https://www.interexchange.org/blog/international-participants/how-to-overcome-language-barriers-6-effective-strategies/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': 'All citations failed to fetch valid content from ContentScraper.', 'motivation': 'A proactive attitude directly contributes to overcoming language and cultural barriers because by actively seeking out new experiences, individuals are more likely to immerse themselves in different cultures and languages. This immersion naturally leads to the development of stronger language skills and a deeper understanding of cultural nuances, making the barriers themselves positive opportunities for growth.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'judge_verdict': 'NO_CITATION', 'spurious_motivation': 'A proactive attitude directly contributes to overcoming language and cultural barriers because by actively seeking out new experiences, individuals are more likely to immerse themselves in different cultures and languages. This immersion naturally leads to the development of stronger language skills and a deeper understanding of cultural nuances, making the barriers themselves positive opportunities for growth.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

