ngthen cognitive mechanisms (self-regulation, delay discounting, future thinking) that improve decision-making and sustaining healthy behavior. However, the citation does not provide the specific physiological/neurochemical details claimed (e.g., increased endorphins, improved metabolic function leading to enhanced cognitive flexibility and motivation) nor direct evidence that those biochemical changes cause a more proactive attitude."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Proactive attitude is positively associated with healthy lifestyle due to the physiological benefits of regular engagement in health-promoting behaviors. As individuals maintain a healthy lifestyle, such as consistent physical activity and nutritious eating, they experience biochemical changes—such as increased endorphin levels and improved metabolic function—that directly enhance cognitive flexibility and motivation. These neurobiological adaptations subsequently foster a more proactive attitude, as individuals become neurologically primed to initiate and sustain positive actions, creating a reinforcing cycle between healthy lifestyle and proactive attitude.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Proactive attitude is positively associated with healthy lifestyle due to the physiological benefits of regular engagement in health-promoting behaviors. As individuals maintain a healthy lifestyle, such as consistent physical activity and nutritious eating, they experience biochemical changes—such as increased endorphin levels and improved metabolic function—that directly enhance cognitive flexibility and motivation. These neurobiological adaptations subsequently foster a more proactive attitude, as individuals become neurologically primed to initiate and sustain positive actions, creating a reinforcing cycle between healthy lifestyle and proactive attitude.',