1089. Willingness of social network-[POSITIVE]->Informal care
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Willingness of social network causes informal care in a direct causal relationship. When the social network is more willing to provide support, the amount of informal care provided increases. Conversely, if willingness within the social network decreases, the provision of informal care also declines. This effect is direct and not mediated by other variables in the CLD.', 'session_id': '62897d48-baff-417b-a11c-f996ae0fb098', 'prob_std': 0.24379193530429133, 'citations': ['https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2024.1446246/full', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK585650/', 'https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/17437199.2022.2032259', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167629609001209'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7982650287903882, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2024.1446246/full", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article analyzes how informal social support (financial help, contact, household assistance, etc.) affects older adults\' mental health and examines mediators like life satisfaction and social participation. It does not measure or test \\"willingness of the social network\\" as an outcome, nor does it present evidence that higher levels of informal care cause network members to become more willing to provide care. While the paper discusses cultural norms (e.g., filial piety) and roles of family ties, it provides no empirical support for the claimed causal pathway from amount of informal care → increased willingness of the social network."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK585650/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited chapter describes concepts of social support, types/functions of network support, and th