   Properties: {'session_id': '62897d48-baff-417b-a11c-f996ae0fb098', 'prob_std': 0.24009178441808285, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1046/j.1365-2710.2001.00363.x', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10001153/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7584088235306324, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review explicitly defines \\"therapeutic compliance\\" (and discusses measurement and types of non-compliance) and even lists behaviors related to delaying or failing to seek care (e.g., \\"delaying in seeking healthcare\\", \\"non‑participation in clinic visits\\"). Thus the claim that there is \\"no information provided about the definitions or measurements of \'Therapy compliance\' and \'Healthcare avoidance\'\\" is contradicted by the source. The review does not, however, establish or evaluate a causal link between therapy compliance and a distinct construct labeled \\"healthcare avoidance,\\" but that does not validate the explanation\'s stated lack of definitional information. Overall the citation does not support the assertion. \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10001153/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article explicitly defines therapeutic adherence/compliance, describes measurement methods (pill counts, MARS, MMAS-8, DAI‑10, etc.), and discusses behaviors such as missed appointments, discharge against medical advice, and reduced use of scheduled services as aspects/consequences of nonadherence. Those items relate directly to healthcare-avoidance behaviors and link adherence to healthcare use outcomes (e.g., appointment attendance, emergency service use, rehospitalization). Therefore the claim that “no information” exists about definitions or measurements and that no causal relationship can be determined is contradicted by the citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "There is no information provided about the definitions or measurements of 'Therapy compliance' and 'Healthcare avoidance'. Without clear definitions, a causal relationship between these variables cannot be determined.", 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2789105739028221, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8349333323148425, 'min_prob': 0.15457532293838655, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0027460965567323798, 'prob_variance': 0.05764406494505917, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7699463704401842, 'avg_nll': 0.2460086013898217}

