 the claim that there is no relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.hhs.nd.gov/sites/www/files/documents/BH/cuijpers_2019_annurev-clinpsy-common-factors.pdf", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review emphasizes that psychotherapy effects and mechanisms are complex, that causal mechanisms are largely unknown, and that observed associations are often correlational or mediated rather than directly causal. That general argument supports the plausibility of “no direct causal link” and that associations would be indirect or mediated. However, the article does not discuss “therapy compliance” or “organizational structure” specifically, nor provide direct evidence about a lack of causal link between those two particular variables. Therefore the citation partially supports the general methodological claim but does not directly support the specific relationship asserted."}], "aggregate_score": 0.16666666666666666, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Therapy compliance does not cause organizational structure to change, nor does organizational structure causally depend on therapy compliance in a direct way. There is no clear causal mechanism by which one directly affects the other, given their definitions and available mediators in the system. Any association between these variables would be indirect or mediated by other factors, not a direct causal link.', 'aggregate_score': 0.16666666666666666, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.4797692430797793, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7776869124283851, 'min_prob': 0.06405577449630884, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003569609880859638, 'prob_variance': 0.08499810320352792, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0845831576613034, 'avg_nll': 0.391886158781743}

