lead people to develop healthier habits (better sleep, exercise, nutrition, hygiene, self-control and mental-health practices) and feel empowered to replace substance use with positive routines. That supports the claim that overcoming addiction can strengthen commitment to healthy behaviors. However, the source discusses changes during/after recovery rather than asserting that chronic addiction itself typically makes people more health‑aware or directly motivates them to adopt healthier lifestyles, so the motivation is only partially supported."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Chronic addiction often leads individuals to become more aware of their health, motivating them to adopt a healthier lifestyle as a form of self-improvement. The experience of overcoming addiction can also strengthen one's commitment to positive habits and wellness practices, thereby fostering a healthy lifestyle.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': "Chronic addiction often leads individuals to become more aware of their health, motivating them to adopt a healthier lifestyle as a form of self-improvement. The experience of overcoming addiction can also strengthen one's commitment to positive habits and wellness practices, thereby fostering a healthy lifestyle.", 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

