   Properties: {'session_id': 'c64355cf-7020-4490-95cf-93a2ccf65a3e', 'prob_std': 0.23168388111101712, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/causal-relationship', 'https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/health-products-compliance-guidance'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7997523300865643, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited review explicitly defines therapeutic compliance and documents multiple therapy-related factors that involve equipment (difficulty using inhalers, CPAP adherence, nebulizer/home devices, packaging aids, requirements for drug storage), and shows these device/handling issues affect adherence. Thus the claim that no information is provided about \\"Therapy compliance\\" or equipment-related effects is contradicted by the sources."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/causal-relationship", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The sole cited source returns an error message and provides no usable content about \\"Equipment\\" or \\"Therapy compliance.\\" Because the citation contains no information, it does not support any causal relationship, so the claim of no relationship (due to lack of information/definitions) is supported by the citation."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/health-products-compliance-guidance", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The FTC guidance does not define or measure the variables \\"Equipment\\" or \\"Therapy compliance.\\" It emphasizes that health-related claims must be clearly specified and substantiated with relevant, validated measures and competent scientific evidence, implying that without definitions and measurement/cont