   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Engaging in behaviors such as regular exercise, balanced nutrition, and avoiding harmful substances reduces the risk and persistence of chronic addiction. Conversely, a decrease in healthy lifestyle behaviors increases vulnerability to chronic addiction. This relationship is inverse and direct, not merely correlational.', 'session_id': 'c64355cf-7020-4490-95cf-93a2ccf65a3e', 'prob_std': 0.24676938970010928, 'citations': ['https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002149.htm', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7148629348402149, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The Mayo Clinic source identifies environmental and peer-group exposure as important risk factors for initiating drug use and advises avoiding high‑risk situations and former drug-using social circles to prevent relapse. That supports the idea that reduced exposure via social environments can lower addiction risk. However, the source does not claim that a \\"healthy lifestyle\\" per se causally eliminates exposure, nor does it assert that reduced exposure (rather than physiological or psychological mechanisms) is the sole or primary reason for lower chronic addiction."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002149.htm", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The MedlinePlus article links healthy behaviors (nutrition, physical activity, rest, and engaging in support/counseling) with improved recovery and lower likelihood of relapse, supporting a negative relationship between a healthy lifestyle and substance use/addiction. However, the citation does not support the motivation\'s claimed mechanism (that reduced exposure via restricting social interactions is the direct cause). The source emphasizes physiological and psychological/behavioral recovery factors (nutrition improving mood, restoring health, and reducing relapse risk) and does not discuss avoidance of environments or social circles as the primary mechanism."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The Cleveland Clinic source identifies exposure/easy access and social pressure as risk factors for substance use disorder and recommends healthy coping activities (exercise, hobbies) to reduce risk, which supports the general idea that lifestyle and reduced exposure can lower risk of addiction. However, the source does not provide direct evidence that investing time in healthy behaviors causally reduces chronic addiction primarily by restricting social interactions or that reduced opportunity for exposure is the sole mechanism; it also emphasizes brain-based, psychological, and other factors in SUD development."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The Cleveland Clinic source identifies environmental factors — especially access to substances and substance use by peers/household members — as important risk factors for addiction and recommends healthy coping (exercise, meditation, hobbies) to reduce risk. That supports the general claim that healthier behaviors can lower addiction risk and that reduced exposure/opportunity matters. However, the source does not provide direct evidence that committing to a healthy lifestyle causally reduces addiction specifically by restricting social interactions to others who engage in healthy habits (the proposed exposure mechanism), so the exact causal pathway asserted in the motivation is not established by the citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease because individuals who invest significant time and energy into maintaining healthy behaviors are less likely to encounter environments or social circles where addictive substances are available. The commitment to a Healthy lifestyle essentially removes exposure to risk factors for Chronic addiction by restricting social interactions to only those who also engage in healthy habits. Therefore, it is the reduced opportunity for exposure, rather than any physiological or psychological mechanism, that directly leads to lower levels of Chronic addiction among those adhering to a Healthy lifestyle.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease because individuals who invest significant time and energy into maintaining healthy behaviors are less likely to encounter environments or social circles where addictive substances are available. The commitment to a Healthy lifestyle essentially removes exposure to risk factors for Chronic addiction by restricting social interactions to only those who also engage in healthy habits. Therefore, it is the reduced opportunity for exposure, rather than any physiological or psychological mechanism, that directly leads to lower levels of Chronic addiction among those adhering to a Healthy lifestyle.', 'perplexity': 1.3554494909016919, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8048516824590491, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.04028507003715813, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0032869299953729924, 'prob_variance': 0.060895131692964406, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9180510299427818, 'avg_nll': 0.30413312692495276}

653. Healthy lifestyle-[NEGATIVE]->Acute care demand leading to an ED visit
