   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication does not cause Equipment, nor does Equipment cause Incorrect use of medication. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables in either direction. No mediating variables in the CLD establish a direct causal path between them. Therefore, there is no causal relationship.', 'session_id': 'c64355cf-7020-4490-95cf-93a2ccf65a3e', 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/', 'https://psnet.ahrq.gov/primer/medication-administration-errors', 'https://home.ecri.org/blogs/ismp-alerts-and-articles-library/implement-strategies-to-prevent-persistent-medication-errors-and-hazards-2024', 'https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/medication-errors-related-cder-regulated-drug-products', 'https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The StatPearls article discusses types, causes, and patient/system harms of medication errors and prevention strategies, but it does not report or provide evidence that incorrect medication use produces chemical residues that corrode or damage medical equipment or that such misuse shortens device lifespan or reliability. The cited content does not address equipment malfunction from medication residues."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://psnet.ahrq.gov/primer/medication-administration-errors", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation is an error page (CloudFront 403) and contains no substantive information about medication use or medical equipment; therefore it does not support or contradict the claimed relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://home.ecri.org/blogs/ismp-alerts-and-articles-library/implement-strategies-to-prevent-persistent-medication-errors-and-hazards-2024", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The ISMP article discusses medication administration errors (e.g., BCMA workarounds, wrong‑route administration with syringes) and impacts of drug/supply shortages, but it does not provide evidence that improper drug administration leaves chemical residues that corrode or damage medical equipment or that such misuse shortens device lifespan. The cited content addresses safety risks to patients and device compatibility/workflow issues, not chemical corrosion or equipment malfunction from residue."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/medication-errors-related-cder-regulated-drug-products", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The FDA citation addresses medication errors, their prevention, labeling/packaging, and surveillance (including human factors and device usability to reduce errors). It does not provide evidence that incorrect medication use leaves chemical residues that corrode or otherwise physically damage medical equipment or shorten device lifespan. The specific causal claim about residues causing equipment malfunction is not supported by the cited content."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The AMCP source discusses types, causes, costs, and prevention of medication errors and refers generally to \\"drug and drug device related problems,\\" but it does not provide any evidence or examples that improper medication administration leaves chemical residues that corrode or damage medical equipment or that misuse shortens device lifespan. The cited content does not address the claimed causal pathway."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication causes medical equipment t