   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers do not directly cause multi-morbidity, nor does multi-morbidity directly cause language and cultural barriers. While associations may exist due to mediators like health literacy or care avoidance behavior, there is no direct causal link between these two variables.', 'session_id': 'c64355cf-7020-4490-95cf-93a2ccf65a3e', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7786751/', 'https://www.qualityhealth.org/wpsc/2017/10/13/impact-of-language-cultural-barriers-on-patient-safety-health-equity/', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32423835/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9896124/', 'https://med.uc.edu/landing-pages/uccom-tribunal/com-chronicles/exploration-of-medicine/2022/09/01/healthcare-standards-across-language-barriers'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7786751/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article discusses how language and cultural discordance impair communication, trust, access, and quality of care (which can affect health service use and clinical management). It does not provide evidence that these barriers directly produce physiological stress responses that weaken immune function or biologically predispose people to develop multiple chronic diseases irrespective of other social or lifestyle factors."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9896124/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article documents that language (and related cultural) barriers impede access to care, cause misdiagnosis, and reduce use of health services — pathways that can worsen health and contribute to poorer outcomes. However, the sources do not provide evidence for the specific biological mechanism claimed (that these barriers directly trigger physiological stress responses that weaken immunity and thereby cause multi‑morbidity), nor do they support the strong claim that such biological predisposition occurs regardless of other social or lifestyle factors."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.qualityhealth.org/wpsc/2017/10/13/impact-of-language-cultural-barriers-on-patient-safety-health-equity/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article documents that language and cultural barriers worsen access, increase medical errors, reduce preventive care (e.g., lower colorectal screening), and contribute to worse health outcomes and disparities — supporting a positive link between these barriers and poorer health. It does not, however, present evidence that these barriers directly cause physiological stress responses that weaken the immune system, nor that they biologically and inevitably predispose individuals to multi-morbidity regardless of other social or lifestyle factors. Those specific biological causal claims are unaddressed by the citation."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32423835/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source discusses difficulties in intercultural health communication and strategies to mitigate language and cultural barriers to reduce health disparities. It does not provide evidence that these barriers directly cause physiological stress responses, weaken the immune system, or biologically predispose individuals to develop multi-morbidity regardless of other factors."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://med.uc.edu/landing-pages/uccom-tribunal/com-chronicles/exploration-of-medicine/2022/09/01/healthcare-standards-across-language-barriers", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article documents that language and cultural barriers impair communication, access, satisfaction, and can lead to misdiagnosis, adverse events, and greater healthcare use. It does not present evidence that these barriers directly cause physiological stress responses that weaken the immune system or biologically predispose individuals to develop multiple chronic diseases regardless of other factors."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers directly increase the risk of multi-morbidity by causing physiological stress responses that weaken the immune system. Over time, individuals facing these barriers are biologically predisposed to develop multiple chronic diseases, regardless of other social or lifestyle factors.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers directly increase the risk of multi-morbidity by causing physiological stress responses that weaken the immune system. Over time, individuals facing these barriers are biologically predisposed to develop multiple chronic diseases, regardless of other social or lifestyle factors.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

