re similar backgrounds. These barriers often encourage people to rely more on family and close-knit social networks, thereby increasing the prevalence and quality of informal care within those groups. As a result, language and cultural differences strengthen support systems and informal caregiving.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

