829. Language and cultural barriers-[NEGATIVE]->Knowledge
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause knowledge to decrease in a direct causal relationship. When language and cultural barriers increase, they hinder effective communication and information transfer, resulting in reduced knowledge acquisition. Conversely, decreasing these barriers facilitates knowledge gains. This relationship is direct and does not require mediation by other listed variables.', 'session_id': 'c64355cf-7020-4490-95cf-93a2ccf65a3e', 'prob_std': 0.2979872887226668, 'citations': ['https://www.redalyc.org/journal/279/27962177008/html/', 'https://www.redalyc.org/journal/279/27962050034/html/', 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/392502522_Language_Barriers_And_Their_Impact_On_Effective_Communication_In_Different_Fields'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.768952602396283, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.redalyc.org/journal/279/27962177008/html/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited literature clearly supports a negative link in that language and cultural barriers impede effective communication, block the flow of information, and in some cases prevent people from seeking necessary information (e.g., Meuter et al.; the review’s numerous examples of misunderstandings, missed information, and reduced information-seeking). However, the specific causal mechanism asserted in the motivation — that barriers increase a culturally based sense of self-sufficiency (belief that existing knowledge is sufficient), which directly and independently reduces motivation to acquire knowledge — is not documented in the provided sources. The citations instead describe multiple mediating processes (misunderstanding, emotional/cognitive responses, identity/trust effects, translation problems, etc.), not the claimed self-sufficiency belief or a direct, mediator-free effect."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.redalyc.o