e does not claim that increasing barriers overall enhances accessibility of information, nor does it support the speculative claim that reducing barriers would decrease incentive to innovate or could limit accessibility over time."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers can enhance the accessibility of information by prompting organizations and institutions to develop more targeted and comprehensive communication strategies. As language and cultural barriers increase, entities are incentivized to produce multilingual resources and culturally tailored materials, which ultimately broadens the range and depth of accessible information available to diverse populations. Reducing these barriers, therefore, may inadvertently decrease the motivation to innovate and diversify informational resources, potentially limiting accessibility over time.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers can enhance the accessibility of information by prompting organizations and institutions to develop more targeted and comprehensive communication strategies. As language and cultural barriers increase, entities are incentivized to produce multilingual resources and culturally tailored materials, which ultimately broadens the range and depth of accessible information available to diverse populations. Reducing these barriers, therefore, may inadvertently decrease the motivation to innovate and diversify informational resources, potentially limiting accessibility over time.', 'perplexity': 1.2349509941155574, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8572343078818404, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.15697846294178686, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004529718967957584, 'prob_variance': 0.05078723747441716, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.743789357969868, 'avg_nll': 0.211