1091. Willingness of social network-[POSITIVE]->Informal care
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Willingness of social network causes informal care in a direct causal relationship. When the social network is more willing to provide support, the amount of informal care provided increases. Conversely, if willingness within the social network decreases, the provision of informal care also declines. This effect is direct and not mediated by other variables in the CLD.', 'session_id': 'c64355cf-7020-4490-95cf-93a2ccf65a3e', 'prob_std': 0.24379193530429133, 'citations': ['https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2024.1446246/full', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK585650/', 'https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/17437199.2022.2032259', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167629609001209'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7982650287903882, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2024.1446246/full", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article analyzes how informal social support (care received) affects older adults’ mental health and examines mediators (life satisfaction, medical access, social participation). It does not measure or test whether greater amounts of informal care cause increased \\"willingness of the social network\\" to participate; nor does it present evidence that provision of care directly raises network members’ willingness. The paper even discusses possible reverse causality (dependence leading to more support), so the specific causal claim in the motivation is not supported by the provided source."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK585650/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited chapter describes concepts of social support, social networks, and functions such as the \\"opportunity for nurturance\\" (i.e., providing