 treatment’s effectiveness, thereby increasing their intrinsic motivation to comply. Conversely, if willingness of social network is low, patients may view the therapy as less reputable or valuable, leading to reduced therapy compliance. The mechanism operates through the social network’s willingness directly shaping patients’ beliefs about treatment potency.', 'perplexity': 7.2694682833356e+58, 'mean_token_prob': 0.733139744674531, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0073403323889259025, 'prob_variance': 0.09240983903500002, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.258375021095091, 'avg_nll': 135.53361854405705}

