1158. Time-[POSITIVE]->Spatial Scale
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Time does not cause Spatial Scale, nor does Spatial Scale cause Time. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables, as one measures temporal duration and the other measures physical extent. Without a specific context or defined mechanism, no causal relationship exists between them.', 'session_id': 'c64355cf-7020-4490-95cf-93a2ccf65a3e', 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK222250/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/veterinary-science-and-veterinary-medicine/temporal-scale', 'https://www.researchgate.net/figure/The-relationship-between-spatial-scale-and-temporal-scale-As-the-spatial-scale-of-a_fig1_353124574', 'https://www.auctoresonline.org/article/re-print-understanding-spatial-and-temporal-scale-in-biology'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK222250/", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited chapter explicitly discusses links between temporal and spatial scales in ecological and climatic phenomena, noting that longer-term changes (e.g., glacial–interglacial transitions and multi-century to millennial processes) produce much larger spatial consequences such as huge range shifts or extinctions. It therefore supports the claim that increasing temporal scale is associated with larger spatial-scale processes."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/veterinary-science-and-veterinary-medicine/temporal-scale", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The only cited source returns an error message and provides no substantive content. There is no evidence in the provided citation to support (or contradict) the claimed positive relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/figure/The-relationship-between-spatial-scale-and-temporal-scale-As-the-spatial-scale-of-a_fig1_353124574", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation is an inaccessible ResearchGate page that returns an error/ access denied message and contains no substantive content or evidence. There is no usable material in the citation to confirm the claimed positive relationship between time and spatial scale."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.auctoresonline.org/article/re-print-understanding-spatial-and-temporal-scale-in-biology", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article explicitly discusses how temporal and spatial scales in biology are intertwined — e.g., that emergent, macroscopic cellular behaviors require time to develop and that choosing a fast temporal resolution can \\"preclude analysis of biological phenomena beyond a cluster of cells.\\" This supports the general idea that longer timeframes can reveal larger-scale biological processes. However, the source is confined to biological examples and does not provide the broad, cross-domain claim or the geological example (continental drift over millions of years) used in the motivation, so the motivation is only partially supported by the citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.375, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'As time increases, the spatial scale of observed phenomena also increases because longer timeframes allow for larger spatial processes to unfold. For example, processes that occur over millions of years, such as continental drift, naturally operate at much larger spatial scales than those occurring over seconds or minutes.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.375, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'As time increases, the spatial scale of observed phenomena also increases because longer timeframes allow for larger spatial processes to unfold. For example, processes that occur